# Test Authentication API
# Use this file with REST Client extension in VS Code or similar tools

### Health Check
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/health

### Register User
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-01-01",
  "nationality": "American",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "phone": "+1234567890",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "homeAddress": "123 Main St, City, Country"
}

### Login User
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Get User Profile (Replace with actual access token)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Refresh Token (Replace with actual refresh token)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

### Logout (Replace with actual refresh token)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "YOUR_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE"
}

### Logout All Devices (Replace with actual access token)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE